  "notes": [
    "How it works: real Minecraft 26.3 runs next to GTA V Legacy story mode and is drawn into it. GTA's movement and camera drive Steve, blocks you place become GTA props, and TNT and creepers blow up in both games.",
    "Press Play: Minecraft starts first. Load a single-player world in Minecraft first (the mod opens its own void creative world \"passthrough\" by itself) and leave its window open. GTA V then starts with BattlEye off: pick Story Mode yourself. GTA shows \"Minecraft passthrough connected\" when linked.",
    "Keys: F7 turns the passthrough off and on. F8 re-levels the Minecraft ground. Left/right mouse are Minecraft's attack/use, mouse wheel or 1-9 the hotbar, Tab an experimental gun mode, Space takes off with the elytra. Walking, driving and the camera stay GTA's.",
    "You need GTA V Legacy on Steam (GTA5.exe, build 3889; not the Enhanced edition) and Minecraft: Java Edition, on Windows. Install ScriptHookV for your GTA build yourself: copy ScriptHookV.dll and dinput8.dll from its bin folder into the GTA V folder.",
    "Needs a GTA V Story Mode save past the prologue: press F7 to turn the mod off, play the opening mission, then press F7 again in Los Santos. Story mode only, never GTA Online: BattlEye stays off while installed. Back up your saves first.",
    "Plays best windowed 1920x1080 with \"Pause game on focus loss\" and depth of field off; first person is smoother than third person. The local link has no password while Minecraft runs. Beta: report bugs to the author with the Report a bug link."
  ]
